From 66ea880c51511b25a7ed6c32f85ad0991ba6a1a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(desktop): port upstream tests to fork behaviour; keep
 empty profile sections [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the upstream merge 13 vitest files failed that pass on both parents. One was a lost
upstream feature: the fork counts its default 'hide automated' view as a narrowing filter, so
upstream's empty-profile sidebar sections (47f0fc99d2d) never showed. The sidebar now passes a
narrowing that ignores the automated default.

The rest are upstream tests that predate fork behaviour and are ported, not weakened:
- ⌘⇧N is session.newSameGateway and ⌘⇧P session.moveToProject in the browser-defaults table;
  the shortcut row label is the fork's 'New session on saved gateway'.
- rows carry a fresh kanban_observed_at (the fork keeps unverified rows 'background' and defers
  turnDone notifications without one).
- @/hermes mocks export getApiRequestConnection/Profile (onboarding scope capture).
- archive mutations get a runtime snapshot; archive waits for its linked-work check.
- onboarding is marked decided before a requested recovery (upstream onboarding-presence gate).
- remote-warm-dispatch drops spawnPriority, retired upstream with the local pool (c63d465dbc2).
---
diff --git a/apps/desktop/electron/remote-warm-dispatch.test.ts b/apps/desktop/electron/remote-warm-dispatch.test.ts
index 356e6d0ca9d76a1d115616025097f5112eaeef65..751f0bac85d41b883cd4ba1f0c34920faebdb59c 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/electron/remote-warm-dispatch.test.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/electron/remote-warm-dispatch.test.ts
@@ -262,7 +262,8 @@ describe('main.ts wiring', () => {
 
   it('prewarms registry SSH connections through ensureRegistryBackend with a forced keepalive probe', () => {
     expect(main).toMatch(/connection\.kind === 'ssh'/)
-    expect(main).toMatch(/ensureRegistryBackend\(connectionId, profile, '', \{ forceProbe, spawnPriority: 'background' \}\)/)
+    // Upstream retired spawn priorities with the local-backend pool (c63d465dbc2).
+    expect(main).toMatch(/ensureRegistryBackend\(connectionId, profile, '', \{ forceProbe \}\)/)
     expect(main).toMatch(/prewarmTargets\(\n\s+readDesktopConnectionsRegistry\(\)/)
   })
 
